        "content": "<p>As another example we can use <code>eval_det</code> to compute the determinant of the map used in the recent counterexample to the Jacobian conjecture.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Tactic.NormDet</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.PDeriv</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv_natCast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map_natCast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv_C</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv_ofNat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">n.AtLeastTwo</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ofNat</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv_natCast</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"x\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"y\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"z\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">z</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix.det</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">!!</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₃</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₃</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₃</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">P₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P₃</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv_ofNat</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">eval_det</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 613602151,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Cadman",
        "timestamp": 1785402735
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are you going to come and demo it on Friday at LLL or are the MI working you too hard? :-) Are there determinants involving matrices associated with the E_8 lattice or the Leech lattice which the sphere packing group could use help in computing?</p>",
        "id": 613604915,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1785403662
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/.60norm_det.60.20and.20.60eval_det.60.20determinant.20tactic/near/613604915\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Are you going to come and demo it on Friday at LLL or are the MI working you too hard? :-) Are there determinants involving matrices associated with the E_8 lattice or the Leech lattice which the sphere packing group could use help in computing?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'll be there to give a demo and explain the implementation a bit at LLL tomorrow! </p>\n<p>I used the tactic to fill some <code>proof_wanted</code> lemmas in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/e4c91783ca8e6a7c693ae624ade32fd22d4e43c1/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Cartan.lean#L263-L270\">LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Cartan.lean</a> but it'd be great to find some other places we could use it.</p>",
        "id": 613605866,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Cadman",
        "timestamp": 1785403985
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The only determinant I see in Sphere Packing is <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/blob/154909fd8954556e5fd9478b0ac6719629c50790/SpherePacking/Basic/E8.lean#L258\">https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/blob/154909fd8954556e5fd9478b0ac6719629c50790/SpherePacking/Basic/E8.lean#L258</a> (which seems to be a basis for the E8 lattice) but it's lower-triangular so their determinant is easy. Of course <code>eval_det</code> would still crush it!</p>",
        "id": 613610639,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1785405704
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"240862\">Oliver Nash</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/.60norm_det.60.20and.20.60eval_det.60.20determinant.20tactic/near/613610639\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The only determinant I see in Sphere Packing is <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/blob/154909fd8954556e5fd9478b0ac6719629c50790/SpherePacking/Basic/E8.lean#L258\">https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/blob/154909fd8954556e5fd9478b0ac6719629c50790/SpherePacking/Basic/E8.lean#L258</a> (which seems to be a basis for the E8 lattice) but it's lower-triangular so their determinant is easy. Of course <code>eval_det</code> would still crush it!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yup, I specifically picked a lower-triangular basis to make the determinant calculation here easy, and instead the work moves into proving it is actually a basis for E8.</p>",
        "id": 613662868,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1785422324
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Interesting: our lack of determinant tactic was shaping things invisibly.</p>",
        "id": 613927329,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1785525471
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I disagree here actually: My original hope was that we'd get a determinant tactic which worked by doing an LU decomposition, which should be fast for ground (ie not symbolic) matrices, and I therefore deliberately picked triangular matrices in the hope that it would make it easier to apply in that case. So I'd instead say that my aspirational design for a determinant tactic was shaping things instead!</p>",
        "id": 614102494,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1785608661
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This still is implicitly shaped by the lack of a <em>fast-enough</em> determinant tactic on arbitrary matrices, right? <span aria-label=\"eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f440\" role=\"img\" title=\"eyes\">:eyes:</span>Or, more to the point: if both the current determinant tactic and the non-symbolic LU version were available, would you still put the effort in to make it lower-triangular?</p>",
        "id": 614126112,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1785631516
    }
]